{"book":"ratio","bookTitle":"Ratio, rate and proportion","concept":3,"title":"Sharing in a ratio","grades":"Grade 7","goal":"I can share an amount in a given ratio.","teach":"Add the parts to find the total number of parts. Divide the amount by that number to find <b>one part</b>. Then multiply. R200 in the ratio 3 : 5: 8 parts, one part = R25, so the shares are R75 and R125. Check: they add up to R200.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:573px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 441 38\"><rect x=\"2.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"52.0\" height=\"34.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"28.0\" y=\"24.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\"></text><rect x=\"57.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"52.0\" height=\"34.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"83.0\" y=\"24.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\"></text><rect x=\"112.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"52.0\" height=\"34.0\" fill=\"#7A0000\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"138.0\" y=\"24.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\"></text><rect x=\"167.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"52.0\" height=\"34.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"193.0\" y=\"24.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\"></text><rect x=\"222.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"52.0\" height=\"34.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"248.0\" y=\"24.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\"></text><rect x=\"277.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"52.0\" height=\"34.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"303.0\" y=\"24.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\"></text><rect x=\"332.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"52.0\" height=\"34.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"358.0\" y=\"24.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\"></text><rect x=\"387.0\" y=\"2.0\" width=\"52.0\" height=\"34.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"413.0\" y=\"24.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\"></text></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">8 equal parts: 3 for one person, 5 for the other.</div></div>","ex":{"q":"Share R900 in the ratio 2 : 3 : 4.","steps":["Total parts: 2 + 3 + 4 = 9.","One part = R900 ÷ 9 = R100.","Shares: R200, R300 and R400 (total R900 <span style=\"font-family:'TeX Gyre Pagella'\">✓</span>)."]},"watch":"Divide by the total number of parts, not by the number of people.<br><br><b>Problem-solving lens</b><br>Draw a bar with one box per part. Then one box is easy to find.","qs":[{"text":"Share R200 in the ratio 3 : 5.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"First share (R)","a":"75","form":"val","o":null},{"t":"box","label":"Second share (R)","a":"125","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"8 parts of R25.","steps":"1. Formula: one part = total ÷ (sum of the ratio numbers); each share = its ratio number × one part.<br>2. one part = R200 ÷ (3 + 5) = R25<br>3. 3 × R25 = R75 and 5 × R25 = R125"},{"text":"Share 48 sweets in the ratio 5 : 3.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"First share","a":"30","form":"val","o":null},{"t":"box","label":"Second share","a":"18","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"8 parts of 6.","steps":"1. Formula: one part = total ÷ (sum of the ratio numbers); each share = its ratio number × one part.<br>2. one part = 48 ÷ (5 + 3) = 6<br>3. 5 × 6 = 30 and 3 × 6 = 18"},{"text":"Two amounts are in the ratio 3 : 7. The smaller is 21. Find the larger.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Larger","a":"49","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"3 parts = 21.","steps":"1. Formula: one part = total ÷ (sum of the ratio numbers); each share = its ratio number × one part.<br>2. 3 parts = 21, so one part = 21 ÷ 3 = 7<br>3. larger = 7 × 7 = 49"}]}